rty '0'` error. Before the freeze it silently reordered the cart, which is why the list showed up sorted by name after the first render.\n\nI changed it to `[...lines].sort(...)` in `src/OrderSummary.tsx`, so it sorts a copy. Totals, shipping, the empty-cart message and the markup are unchanged. `CartPage` needed no change, because it only reads `lines`, and it now lists them in the order added on every render.\n\nThe regression test is in `tests/OrderSummary.test.tsx`. It renders `OrderSummary` with a fully frozen array of frozen lines, with and without `sortByName`. It checks the rows come out sorted by name in one case and in the given order in the other. It also renders `CartPage` and checks the cart array's order is untouched and the list is in added order.\n\n`vitest` wasn't installed, so I ran `npm install` to run the tests.","ttft_ms":1113,"type":"result","duration_ms":18535,"uuid":"ba2b210e-6e5a-4918-9732-6a934c6585a0","ttft_stream_ms":707,"time_to_request_ms":34,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":8,"system_prompt":9,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":1,"input_attachments":5,"input_hooks":0,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":2,"engine_pickup":0,"autocompact":1,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":1,"client_creation":1,"request_build":2},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":0,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":57,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"first_content_frame_ms":707,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
